  "raw_text": "The session resolved a latent authority_resolution between two candidate session archive formats: the .jsonl files written by Claude Code, and the .gz produced by script -f continuous flush. The .jsonl is structurally richer \u2014 typed messages, tool calls, full metadata \u2014 but carries an occult_dependency on process stability: memory leaks truncate or lose it on crash, and the assertive claim grounded this historically: \"leaks appear gone for now, but they will be back.\" The script -f flush writes continuously to disk, making the .gz the crash-resilient primary. This is a cooperative quality enforcement: the .jsonl offers an illusion of canonical completeness it cannot guarantee under adversarial conditions, while the .gz is honest about what it is \u2014 a terminal recording \u2014 but always present. The harmony_restoration is a clear hierarchy: .gz as crash-resilient archive, .md as legibility twin derived from the reliable source, and .jsonl as bonus metadata when available but not load-bearing.",
